cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  IMbrave150-mock — a synthetic multi-hospital cohort, and a
  reproducible agent-driven analysis of it
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, the course, or the recorded walkthrough,
  please cite it as below. All data are synthetic; cite the original
  trial (see references) for anything clinical.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Hsieh-Ting
    alias: 林協霆
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Medical Oncology, Koo Foundation Sun Yat-Sen Cancer
      Center, Taipei, Taiwan
repository-code: https://github.com/htlin222/IMBrave150-mock
license: MIT
keywords:
  - synthetic data
  - survival analysis
  - propensity score matching
  - target trial emulation
  - reproducible research
  - large language model agents
  - medical education
abstract: >-
  A fully synthetic patient-level dataset that reproduces the published
  summary statistics of the IMbrave150 phase-3 trial, distributed in two
  teaching layers: a randomised cohort of 501 patients, and a confounded
  real-world layer of 1,800 patients split across ten hospitals in three
  incompatible EHR schemas. The repository also contains a 32-mission
  guided course in which an AI coding agent performs the entire analysis
  — harmonisation, propensity-score matching, survival analysis,
  subgroups, a 120-specification curve, TMLE, and manuscript preparation
  with machine-verified citations — together with the verbatim prompt
  list, per-mission acceptance checks, and terminal recordings of
  complete runs. No real patient is represented and nothing in it
  constitutes evidence about any therapy.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Atezolizumab plus Bevacizumab in Unresectable Hepatocellular
      Carcinoma
    authors:
      - family-names: Finn
        given-names: Richard S.
      - family-names: Qin
        given-names: Shukui
      - family-names: Ikeda
        given-names: Masafumi
    journal: New England Journal of Medicine
    year: 2020
    volume: "382"
    issue: "20"
    start: 1894
    end: 1905
    doi: 10.1056/NEJMoa1915745
    notes: >-
      The published trial the synthetic data are calibrated to. This
      repository contains no data from it beyond its printed summary
      statistics.
